#
# Counter-example for math:SeriesShape: a math:Series naming its general term but
# carrying no math:hasConvergence (sh:minCount 1). Validation MUST emit
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:UnderspecifiedConvergence). Bound by
# ex:ecSeriesMissingConvergence.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:divergentSeries a math:Series ;
    math:operator math:summationBinder ;
    math:seriesTerm ex:harmonicTerm .

# The series term is a named operand represented as a math:SymbolReference,
# which supplies a concrete symbolic leaf rather than the abstract
# math:MathematicalExpression base. This fixture also omits a bound declaration and
# body; its ExampleConformance cell pins the minimum-count component and source
# shape, without claiming a sole finding or failure class.
ex:harmonicTerm a math:SymbolReference ; math:hasMathematicalSymbol ex:harmonicTermSymbol .
ex:harmonicTermSymbol a math:MathematicalSymbol .
